cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LiouScope: Beyond the Liouvillian Gap"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file
  together with the references block below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Coworker Research / Coworkerz"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-05-10"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/coworker-research/liouscope"
url: "https://github.com/coworker-research/liouscope"
abstract: >-
  LiouScope is a multi-diagnostic relaxation analysis framework for
  finite-dimensional time-homogeneous Markovian open quantum lattice systems
  (GKSL / QMS). It quantifies when and why the Liouvillian gap fails as a
  relaxation-time predictor, providing twenty diagnostics (D1-D20) organised in
  six layers S/N/R/U/C/G and a twelve-class mechanism taxonomy A1-A12.
keywords:
  - open quantum systems
  - Liouvillian
  - Lindblad
  - GKSL
  - QMS
  - relaxation
  - spectral gap
  - non-normality
  - Mpemba effect
  - quantum simulation
  - reproducibility
